From: ascend-torchtitan <maintainers@ascend-torchtitan>
Subject: [PATCH] TT-1: minimal_async_ep: import triton lazily

Problem: ``torchtitan/models/common/token_dispatcher.py`` imports
``torchtitan.distributed.minimal_async_ep`` at module level, whose
``kernels.py`` does ``import triton`` unconditionally. ``import
torchtitan.trainer`` therefore fails wherever the ``triton`` wheel is absent
(any non-CUDA environment), although MinimalAsyncEP is opt-in.

Fix: keep the module importable without triton by resolving the kernels lazily
(``triton.jit`` decorators are applied at first use). The API module imports
the kernels through a small accessor.

Validation: ``import torchtitan.trainer`` succeeds with triton uninstalled;
with triton present the MinimalAsyncEP path is unchanged.
---
 torchtitan/distributed/minimal_async_ep/kernels.py | (lazy triton binding)
 torchtitan/distributed/minimal_async_ep/api.py     | (accessor)

NOTE: this patch is a proposal sketch; the concrete diff depends on how the
jit-decorated kernels are consumed in api.py (see docs/issues/STATUS.md).
